WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.195 --> 00:00:02.010
(intense music)

00:00:02.010 --> 00:00:03.960
- [George] Lordstown Motors.

00:00:03.960 --> 00:00:05.670
At one point, the company was racing

00:00:05.670 --> 00:00:08.340
to build America's first
all-electric pickup.

00:00:08.340 --> 00:00:10.260
- They make 'em in Lordstown, Ohio.

00:00:10.260 --> 00:00:11.580
I heard the sales are great.

00:00:11.580 --> 00:00:14.640
- It had for a design for a
truck, a factory to make it in,

00:00:14.640 --> 00:00:17.430
and hundreds of millions
of dollars in investment.

00:00:17.430 --> 00:00:20.280
But then, the wheels fell
off Lordstown Motors.

00:00:20.280 --> 00:00:21.810
Its share price plummeted.

00:00:21.810 --> 00:00:24.060
It's namesake factory was sold off,

00:00:24.060 --> 00:00:26.640
and now, the future of
its pickup, the Endurance,

00:00:26.640 --> 00:00:27.600
is in question.

00:00:27.600 --> 00:00:30.739
So what exactly happened
to Lordstown Motors?

00:00:30.739 --> 00:00:33.994
(intense music continues)

00:00:33.994 --> 00:00:35.280
(light music)
Our story starts,

00:00:35.280 --> 00:00:39.870
somewhat unsurprisingly,
here, Lordstown, Ohio, 2019.

00:00:39.870 --> 00:00:42.210
General Motors have been
making the Chevrolet Cruze here

00:00:42.210 --> 00:00:45.360
for years, but a drop in sales
led to the company wanting

00:00:45.360 --> 00:00:46.410
to close the plant,

00:00:46.410 --> 00:00:48.720
which led to protests and drew criticism

00:00:48.720 --> 00:00:50.460
from then President Donald Trump.

00:00:50.460 --> 00:00:51.810
- What's going on with General Motors?

00:00:51.810 --> 00:00:54.150
Get that plant open or sell it to somebody

00:00:54.150 --> 00:00:55.380
and they'll open it.

00:00:55.380 --> 00:00:56.670
- [George] GM did just that.

00:00:56.670 --> 00:01:00.390
They gave a new EV
startup a $40 million loan

00:01:00.390 --> 00:01:04.530
to buy the plant complete with
machinery for $20 million.

00:01:04.530 --> 00:01:05.700
The startup would be named

00:01:05.700 --> 00:01:08.850
after the neighborhood
itself, Lordstown Motors.

00:01:08.850 --> 00:01:10.920
Its founder was the former chief executive

00:01:10.920 --> 00:01:14.220
of another fledgling automotive
startup called Workhorse,

00:01:14.220 --> 00:01:16.592
a man named Steve Burns.

00:01:16.592 --> 00:01:19.480
- We think we're going to
do the impossible here.

00:01:19.480 --> 00:01:21.300
- [George] Burns licensed a vehicle design

00:01:21.300 --> 00:01:23.070
from his former company, Workhorse,

00:01:23.070 --> 00:01:24.660
and set about entering the race

00:01:24.660 --> 00:01:26.880
to build the first EV pickup.

00:01:26.880 --> 00:01:29.730
And remember, this is
before Ford's F-150 Lighting

00:01:29.730 --> 00:01:32.100
or Rivian's R1T had been released.

00:01:32.100 --> 00:01:33.180
- Our first vehicle

00:01:33.180 --> 00:01:35.610
is the Endurance
all-electric pickup truck.

00:01:35.610 --> 00:01:38.100
- Armed with a factory
and a design for a truck,

00:01:38.100 --> 00:01:40.320
all the company needed now was money.

00:01:40.320 --> 00:01:43.500
So in August, Lordstown announced
it intended to go public

00:01:43.500 --> 00:01:46.470
through a merger with a special
purpose acquisition company.

00:01:46.470 --> 00:01:49.710
And investor sentiment
around the company soared,

00:01:49.710 --> 00:01:51.870
lifted, like many others in the EV market,

00:01:51.870 --> 00:01:54.840
by a wave of investors on
the hunt for the next Tesla.

00:01:54.840 --> 00:01:56.790
But also, partly because the company said

00:01:56.790 --> 00:01:59.610
it had around 27,000 pre-orders,

00:01:59.610 --> 00:02:02.880
plus $75 million of investment from GM.

00:02:02.880 --> 00:02:05.850
- The financing that comes
from being publicly listed

00:02:05.850 --> 00:02:07.650
is the last piece we needed

00:02:07.650 --> 00:02:10.467
as we march towards production in 2021.

00:02:10.467 --> 00:02:14.087
- But Lordstown's RIDE was
about to get a lot bumpier.

00:02:14.087 --> 00:02:14.920
(somber music)

00:02:14.920 --> 00:02:17.670
In the early hours of January 13, 2021,

00:02:17.670 --> 00:02:20.430
an Endurance caught fire
on a road in Michigan

00:02:20.430 --> 00:02:23.100
while being tested by Lordstown engineers.

00:02:23.100 --> 00:02:26.100
Lordstown said the fire was
due to nonconforming parts

00:02:26.100 --> 00:02:27.690
on the prototype battery.

00:02:27.690 --> 00:02:30.660
And before long, the company's
share price began to tumble.

00:02:30.660 --> 00:02:32.910
Around that time, several top executives

00:02:32.910 --> 00:02:35.790
at Lordstown sold off
chunks of their own stock,

00:02:35.790 --> 00:02:38.340
though the company later
concluded there was no wrongdoing

00:02:38.340 --> 00:02:40.770
and that the sales were
made for reasons unrelated

00:02:40.770 --> 00:02:42.660
to the performance of the company.

00:02:42.660 --> 00:02:43.620
Then came the bidding

00:02:43.620 --> 00:02:46.290
for a United States
Postal Service contract

00:02:46.290 --> 00:02:48.240
for a fleet of new electric vehicles.

00:02:48.240 --> 00:02:49.950
Now, Lordstown hadn't submitted a bid

00:02:49.950 --> 00:02:51.570
to design and build those trucks,

00:02:51.570 --> 00:02:53.010
but remember Workhorse?

00:02:53.010 --> 00:02:55.710
Well, it had, and it was
expected to manufacture

00:02:55.710 --> 00:02:58.200
those trucks in Lordstown's factory.

00:02:58.200 --> 00:02:59.160
But then...

00:02:59.160 --> 00:03:01.950
- Oshkosh Defense of Oshkosh, Wisconsin

00:03:01.950 --> 00:03:03.780
has been awarded the production contract

00:03:03.780 --> 00:03:07.137
for the Postal Service's next
generation delivery vehicles.

00:03:07.137 --> 00:03:08.700
(attendees applauding)
- Workhorse didn't win,

00:03:08.700 --> 00:03:11.190
and Lordstown's shares tumbled further.

00:03:11.190 --> 00:03:12.830
But it still had further to fall.

00:03:12.830 --> 00:03:13.680
(somber music)

00:03:13.680 --> 00:03:17.100
In March, short seller Hindenburg
Research accused Lordstown

00:03:17.100 --> 00:03:19.920
of misleading investors
on, among other things,

00:03:19.920 --> 00:03:21.690
how firm its pre-orders were.

00:03:21.690 --> 00:03:24.240
Saying that many of them
were largely fictitious.

00:03:24.240 --> 00:03:25.110
The report led

00:03:25.110 --> 00:03:27.780
to a Securities and
Exchange Commission inquiry,

00:03:27.780 --> 00:03:30.180
and later, a Justice
Department investigation.

00:03:30.180 --> 00:03:32.100
And although then CEO, Steve Burns,

00:03:32.100 --> 00:03:34.290
told "WSJ" in March 2021

00:03:34.290 --> 00:03:36.840
that the report contained
half-truths and lies

00:03:36.840 --> 00:03:39.330
and denied misrepresenting the order book,

00:03:39.330 --> 00:03:41.340
he eventually resigned
after a board committee

00:03:41.340 --> 00:03:43.980
found inaccuracies in
the company's pre-orders.

00:03:43.980 --> 00:03:45.810
I tried to reach Burns for comment,

00:03:45.810 --> 00:03:47.220
but I was unable to do so.

00:03:47.220 --> 00:03:49.020
Finally, by the middle of 2021,

00:03:49.020 --> 00:03:51.090
the company announced that
it didn't have enough funds

00:03:51.090 --> 00:03:53.100
to begin full commercial production.

00:03:53.100 --> 00:03:55.547
Lordstown needed money, fast.

00:03:55.547 --> 00:03:56.640
(mysterious music)

00:03:56.640 --> 00:04:00.840
Enter Foxconn, yep, the
Taiwanese iPhone manufacturer.

00:04:00.840 --> 00:04:03.270
The company had said it had
ambitions to assemble EVs

00:04:03.270 --> 00:04:06.240
for a variety of customers
on a contract basis,

00:04:06.240 --> 00:04:07.890
much like it does with its phones.

00:04:07.890 --> 00:04:10.740
Foxconn wanted a factory and
Lordstown needed capital,

00:04:10.740 --> 00:04:12.810
so the two companies struck an agreement.

00:04:12.810 --> 00:04:16.050
Lordstown would sell its
namesake factory to Foxconn

00:04:16.050 --> 00:04:17.970
for $230 million,

00:04:17.970 --> 00:04:20.670
and Foxconn would build
Lordstown's vehicle.

00:04:20.670 --> 00:04:22.290
That was the plan anyway.

00:04:22.290 --> 00:04:25.500
Production finally started for awhile

00:04:25.500 --> 00:04:27.131
and then stopped again shortly after

00:04:27.131 --> 00:04:29.130
when the company found a problem with some

00:04:29.130 --> 00:04:30.330
of its electrical connectors.

00:04:30.330 --> 00:04:31.440
- [Edward] We filed paperwork

00:04:31.440 --> 00:04:34.080
with the National Highway
Traffic Safety Administration

00:04:34.080 --> 00:04:36.390
to voluntarily recall the Endurance.

00:04:36.390 --> 00:04:40.080
- Lordstown recalled all vehicles
that were out in the wild,

00:04:40.080 --> 00:04:42.240
all 19 of them.

00:04:42.240 --> 00:04:44.310
And shortly after, the
company's share price,

00:04:44.310 --> 00:04:46.830
which at one point had been over $30,

00:04:46.830 --> 00:04:50.610
fell below $1 and stayed
there for more than 30 days,

00:04:50.610 --> 00:04:53.160
triggering a delisting notice from Nasdaq.

00:04:53.160 --> 00:04:55.890
That led to Foxconn saying
that Lordstown has breached

00:04:55.890 --> 00:04:58.890
its agreement and that Foxconn
would back out of the deal

00:04:58.890 --> 00:05:00.630
if the matter wasn't resolved.

00:05:00.630 --> 00:05:01.710
To try and fix the issue,

00:05:01.710 --> 00:05:04.980
Lordstown announced that it was
doing a reverse stock split,

00:05:04.980 --> 00:05:07.440
merging 15 shares into one,

00:05:07.440 --> 00:05:10.500
to try and raise the price above $1.

00:05:10.500 --> 00:05:12.390
Oh, and just before all that happened,

00:05:12.390 --> 00:05:15.060
another Lordstown vehicle caught fire.

00:05:15.060 --> 00:05:17.580
This time, a test vehicle in storage.

00:05:17.580 --> 00:05:19.783
Lordstown said it would
investigate the cause.

00:05:19.783 --> 00:05:20.616
(light music)

00:05:20.616 --> 00:05:22.680
All that brings us to the present day.

00:05:22.680 --> 00:05:25.140
Lordstown has said it hopes
its reverse stock split

00:05:25.140 --> 00:05:27.840
will lead to Foxconn
returning to the deal.

00:05:27.840 --> 00:05:29.880
If Foxconn does, then there may be hope

00:05:29.880 --> 00:05:31.410
for the Endurance yet.

00:05:31.410 --> 00:05:34.920
But if it doesn't and Lordstown
can't find other funding,

00:05:34.920 --> 00:05:36.960
the company says it may seek to file

00:05:36.960 --> 00:05:38.520
for bankruptcy protection.

00:05:38.520 --> 00:05:40.290
I spoke to Foxconn and Lordstown,

00:05:40.290 --> 00:05:42.240
but neither would comment on the deal.

00:05:42.240 --> 00:05:45.570
But within its SEC filings
lies another big hurdle.

00:05:45.570 --> 00:05:48.060
Lordstown says the cost
to build the Endurance

00:05:48.060 --> 00:05:50.940
is currently, and expected
to continue to be,

00:05:50.940 --> 00:05:53.490
substantially higher
than its selling price.

00:05:53.490 --> 00:05:55.980
And that makes what
happens next for Lordstown

00:05:55.980 --> 00:05:57.360
even more challenging.

00:05:57.360 --> 00:05:58.860
In the three years that the company

00:05:58.860 --> 00:06:01.380
has been navigating its
various production woes,

00:06:01.380 --> 00:06:03.390
others, including Ford and Rivian,

00:06:03.390 --> 00:06:06.120
have been delivering their
EV pickups to customers.

00:06:06.120 --> 00:06:09.300
And more trucks, among them
the Chevy Silverado EV,

00:06:09.300 --> 00:06:10.200
are on the way.

00:06:10.200 --> 00:06:14.190
And with the cheapest Silverado
set to be around $20,000

00:06:14.190 --> 00:06:15.840
cheaper than the Endurance,

00:06:15.840 --> 00:06:18.600
not only has Lordstown
lost the race to be first,

00:06:18.600 --> 00:06:20.787
but it may now struggle
to compete altogether.

00:06:20.787 --> 00:06:24.120
(light music continues)

